<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    ROT_LIVE_PREPARATIONS_1, OWNER CARD 6 (RULED 2026-09-17). The whole
    content side of "selling a part of yourself" is this one def.

    THE MECHANISM IS CONTENT-BLIND AND THIS IS THE DATA. The C#
    (RM_Patch_TreasureSaleConscience, mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards)
    names no tea, no symbiont and no thought; it reads
    RM_TreasureMarkerExtension off whatever was sold, matches the tag
    against every RM_TreasureConscienceDef in the load order, and gives that
    def's thought to colonists holding any of ITS carrierHediffs. Adding a
    fourth symbiont or a fifth treasure is an XML edit here and on the item,
    never a code change.

    THE MARKER IS A modExtension, NOT A thingCategory (the ticket left the
    choice open). A thingCategory is also a storage filter and a bill
    ingredient filter: giving the teas a shared category purely to tag them
    would silently reshape every stockpile and recipe filter that matches
    parent categories, and a player reorganizing a freezer would be editing
    the conscience. A DefModExtension has exactly one reader.

    WHY THE WHOLE MayRequire BLOCK. This def's TYPE lives in
    environmentalhazards, so the entire <RimMandrake...RM_TreasureConscienceDef>
    element cannot resolve without that mod. Unlike a comp <li>, a top-level
    def element has no MayRequire — so this file ships the def unguarded and
    the def simply fails to parse (logged, harmless) if the mod is absent,
    exactly as any content def naming a missing type does. The ITEMS
    themselves stay loadable either way because their marker is an <li>
    inside <modExtensions> carrying its own MayRequire.

    minCountSold 1: card 6 does not carve out small sales, and the
    treasures come in units of one-to-three anyway.
  -->

  <RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_TreasureConscienceDef>
    <defName>RUT_RotTreasureConscience</defName>
    <treasureTag>RotTreasure</treasureTag>
    <thought>RUT_SoldRotTreasureMemory</thought>
    <minCountSold>1</minCountSold>
    <affectsAllColonists>true</affectsAllColonists>
    <carrierHediffs>
      <li>RUT_Sym_Quickflesh</li>
      <li>RUT_Sym_Nightwake</li>
      <li>RUT_Sym_Sheenblood</li>
      <li>RUT_Sym_Mycoid</li>
      <li>RUT_SheenSymbiosis</li>
    </carrierHediffs>
  </RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_TreasureConscienceDef>

</Defs>
